<title>SOUTH KOREA: Midopa, Dainong limit-down.</title>
<headline>Midopa, Dainong limit-down.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of South Korea's Midopa Department store and its parent firm Dainong Corp went limit-down in Friday morning trading on news Midopa was the target for a takeover deal, brokers said.</p>
<p>Midopa fell 3,300 won to its limit of 38,200 and Dainong lost 800 won to 9,300.  </p>
<p>Shindongbang Corp on Thursday told the Korea Stock Exchange it was considering a takeover through a public tender offer.</p>
<p>Hours later, Korea Industrial Co announced it was also thinking of making a similar bid for the retailer.</p>
<p>Midopa, a core company in the Dainong Group, operates a chain of fashionable department stores.</p>
<p>Shindongbang's shares were halted for trading until Saturday by the exchange. Korea Industrial's shares fell 1,400 won to its lower limit of 16,700.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom 9822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
